#
# kiwi-cake-lekiwi.service: a USER unit (systemctl --user) for the aarch64 Cake resident of the LeKiwi deployment.
# Its supervisor slot launches and supervises the camera-less motor host (run-host.sh) and its mobile_approach
# capability slot launches the capability process (run-capability.sh) once activated. Rendered on the robot
# computer by bin/pi/lekiwi-deploy.sh install with the two absolute paths filled in, both through the link
# ~/kc-lekiwi/current, which only ever names a VERIFIED release; no sudo, nothing system-wide.
#
# NEVER ENABLED, AND STARTED ONLY BY bin/pi/lekiwi-deploy.sh arm, with the operator present. Starting this unit starts
# the motor host, which attaches to the arm and establishes the base zero-speed hold, and the host wrapper starts the
# host only against the one-shot arm token that arm writes: a restart (Restart= below, or Cake restarting the child)
# finds no token and holds the host. This file deliberately has NO [Install] section: with no WantedBy= there is no
# target to enable it into, so linger can never start it at boot.
#
# The service fields are the ones kiwi-cake-demo.service.in states the reasons for, unchanged:
# Restart=on-abnormal relaunches the resident after a crash as a fresh activation of the Plan its configuration
# names; KillMode=mixed sends the stop signal to the resident only, and the resident stops each child with the
# signal the Plan configured (SIGINT), then a bounded deadline, then force; TimeoutStopSec sits above that bounded
# stop and below the manager's 90-second default. The default KillMode=control-group would SIGTERM the host at the
# same instant, and the pinned LeRobot host has no SIGTERM handler.
[Unit]
Description=kiwi-cake-lekiwi: Cake resident supervising the LeKiwi host and the mobile_approach capability (user unit)

[Service]
Type=simple
ExecStart=@@CAKE_RESIDENT@@ --config @@RESIDENT_CONF@@
Restart=on-abnormal
RestartSec=2
KillMode=mixed
KillSignal=SIGTERM
TimeoutStopSec=60
